-Timeline gap: ~2 months, four interventions. (Note: metallization and
-gate deposition imply resist/bake lithography not itemized in the
-recorded timeline — flagged as a timeline gap, not used in
-classification.) Directional rule in force throughout: documented
-conversion is **ABC→ABA only**.
-
-## Step 4 — Per-region fusion table
-
-| Channel | Transport verdict (now) | Raman verdict (stage S1) | Coverage | Fused verdict + strength | Mechanism class |
-|---|---|---|---|---|---|
-| **ch_A** | ABA (strong) — two SdH tones, partition f_ML+f_BL = F_L within 3%, Onsager-tracking | R1: ABA (strong) — narrow 2D pop. 52.1 ± 2.4 cm⁻¹; single M⁻ | covered | **ABA (strong)** — agreement across independent physics (band structure read electrically and optically); strongest evidence class this recipe produces | **Concordant** |
-| **ch_B** | ABA (weak) — dominant F_L tone + marginal slow shoulder; no D-tunable CNP gap (R_CNP < 4 kΩ at \|D\| ≤ 0.3 V/nm) | R2: ABC (strong) — broad pop. 66.8 ± 2.1 cm⁻¹, Δ = 14.7 cm⁻¹, strain-mimic screen passed; split M⁻ | covered | **ABA (weak)** for the device-now; both calls stand (Raman true at S1, transport true now). Region recorded: **"converted (consistent-with), step: contact metallization 2025-12-01 — C3/C4 leads deposited directly across the region"** (top-tier risk) | **Reconciled-by-conversion** |
-| **ch_C** | ABC (strong) — single F_L tone across n, Luttinger-consistent; R_CNP > 2 MΩ at D = 0.4 V/nm; no crossing chain | R3: ABA (strong) — narrow pop. 51.8 ± 2.6 cm⁻¹ matching R1; terrace screen passed; single M⁻ | covered (partial under worst-case −1.5 µm shift) | **Cannot tell — fork to report.** Raman-ABA vs transport-ABC: conversion cannot explain (would require undocumented ABA→ABC); same-region strong-vs-strong | **Unreconciled** |
