-### ch_B — notes on the conversion row
-
-The class conditions are met exactly: Raman ABC (strong, S1), transport
-ABA (weak, now), and Step 3 names a top-tier risky step *on the region
-itself* (Cr/Au leads across ch_B). Conversion is asserted as
-**consistent-with**, not observed. The competing reading — that
-transport misread and ch_B is still ABC — is exactly the fork transport's
-own hedge allows (slow shoulder is extraction-window-sensitive; ABC "not
-excluded by frequency content alone"); what tips the row to ABA-now is
-the absence of a D-tunable CNP gap. Deciding follow-ups (from the base
-contracts): lower-T spot check + per-branch LK mass split (transport);
-re-map through the encapsulant (Raman).
-
-### ch_C — the unreconciled fork (STYLE rule 14)
-
-Both calls are strong; conversion runs the wrong way; registration
-overlap persists over ≥ 95% of the channel under any admissible shift.
-One modality being wrong is the hypothesis set — misreads each
-contract's hedges already allow:
-
